<!-- Every requirement names the §13 success criterion that would notice its
absence, and this is not bookkeeping.

`.github/scripts/coverage.sh` reports a requirement as "covered" when some plan
lists its id in `covers:`. That is a CLAIM, not a delivery, and nothing
downstream compares the claim to what the plan's slices actually build — a plan
naming twelve requirements and building three passes every gate green, and the
run then walks to acceptance reporting "every requirement is covered by a plan".

docs/acceptance.md is the one artifact in an unattended run whose pull request
requires your review, so it is the single place a failure is guaranteed to reach
you. An S id here is what turns an over-claimed `covers:` into a visible empty
evidence cell instead of a green coverage line. A requirement you cannot name a
criterion for is a requirement nothing will ever check was built. -->

